Under a thrashing routing pattern, an LRU cache of experts experiences frequent eviction of experts due to the rapid switching between different routing patterns, leading to poor performance and instability. The cache's effectiveness is compromised as it continuously replaces experts with less relevant ones, while the system struggles to maintain consistent routing decisions. This results in a cycle where the cache fails to retain useful experts, exacerbating the thrashing behavior and degrading overall system performance.<|im_end|>
